WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.601
[cow mooing]

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:05.372
NARRATOR: Each year after the
harvest, the people of Thebes

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:08.074
held a celebration of the
dead called the "Beautiful

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.175
Festival of the Valley."

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:14.914
They carried statues of
Thebes' three main gods

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.916
in a grand procession
out of Karnak

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.785
temple east of the river.

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.754
[music playing]

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.624
They crossed the Nile in
ceremonial boats following

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:28.361
the sun's journey from the East
Bank, the land of the living,

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:32.832
to the West, the
land of the dead.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:35.502
The procession ended at
the tombs and temples

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:37.904
on the West Bank,
where people had laid

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:40.473
offerings, including
pots of food

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.075
at the graves of the deceased.

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:44.210
[music playing]

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:47.013
[interposing voices]

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:52.552
The ritual ensured the dead
had provisions for eternity.

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:56.156
These pots mean a tomb
should be very close.

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:58.425
[interposing voices]

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:29.122
The roughly carved
casket appears to be

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:32.192
buried in a miniature tomb.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:35.695
This is clearly no king,
but it's a vital clue

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:36.763
that he might be near.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:53.713
If the burial does
predate Amunhotep I,

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:58.485
it proves Dra' Abu el-Naga' was
a cemetery by the time he died.

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:01.154
So he could be buried here.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:04.557
But there's no way to tell
until this coffin is out

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:05.892
of the ground.

